include LICENSE
include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md

# The conformance suite is the artifact another implementation checks itself
# against, so it travels in the sdist even though it is not installed. The
# specification travels for the same reason, and more so: the suite says
# whether an implementation agrees, docs/ say what it is meant to agree with.
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include examples *.ypy
recursive-include docs *.md

# tools/ ships because tests/ depends on it: test_ref_grammar.py imports
# check_ref_grammar to machine-check GRAMMAR §G5 against parse_ref. Without
# it the sdist's suite does not merely lose that test -- it fails to collect,
# so *no* test runs. Caught 2026-09-19 by the release procedure's "run the
# sdist's own tests in a clean venv" step, before it ever shipped.
recursive-include tools *.py
